  "answer": "I'm assuming \"that charge\" means TX-0401. Here are the details from your account:\n\n- **TX-0401**: EUR 240.00 to TechMart Online on 20 July 2026, card, settled\n- **TX-0402**: EUR 240.00 to TechMart Online on 14 July 2026, card, settled\n\nThese are two identical charges to the same merchant, six days apart. If you were charged twice for one purchase, the duplicate-charge route may apply.\n\nTo check whether a dispute can be opened, I need to know which of these describes your situation:\n\n1. **Duplicate charge**: you were billed twice for the same purchase.\n2. **Goods not received**: you paid but did not receive the item.\n3. **Service not rendered**: you paid for a service that was not provided.\n4. **Unauthorized debit**: you did not make or approve this payment.\n5. **Card-not-present fraud**: someone used your card details online without your permission.\n\nTell me which applies and whether you mean TX-0401 or TX-0402. I'll run the eligibility check before anything is filed, and I won't open a dispute until you've confirmed the details.",
